I am trying to write a program that hijacks a car by making it run, but I don't know how to do it. I have an Arduino, a motor shield, and a car with a 12V battery. How can I make the car run by sending a signal to the motor shield? Thanks.
The motor shield has two outputs, one for the right motor and one for the left motor. The output is a PWM signal with a duty cycle between 0 and 100%. The higher the duty cycle, the faster the motor will run.
You can use the Arduino to send a PWM signal to the motor shield and make the car run. Here is an example sketch that will make the car run in a straight line:
